  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Much cooler today, with scattered showers ahead of a \ngradual warm up through the remainder of the week.\n\nA strong cold front will move across the eastern Great Lakes region \nthis morning. Elevated instability and deep moisture will support \nshowers and a few thunderstorms along the front. Cold air advection \nwithin a westerly flow will bring an abrupt airmass change to the \nregion causing 850mb temperatures will fall to +6C by this afternoon \nand limit high temperatures to the 60s to low 70s. Based on past \nsoundings at KBUF, +6C at 850mb is below the 10th percentile and \nnear the daily min for this time of year. Steepening low level lapse \nrates under an upper level trough will support widely scattered \nshowers with lake enhancement focusing showers and lake clouds east-\nsoutheast of the Lakes today. \n\nHigh pressure will build in tonight and reside across the region \nthrough Friday bringing dry weather and a gradual warming trend \nthrough the end of the week.",
